      "text": "I need to be straightforward with you here — and this is important for your academic work.\n\n## I Cannot Summarize This Book\n\nAs established in my previous search, **no verified record of this book, its author, or its publisher exists** across any accessible database, library catalog, or web source. Because I have no confirmed evidence that this work exists, I will not attempt to retrieve or summarize its contents.\n\nSpecifically, I will **not** use content retrieval tools (such as `fetch_book_excerpt`, `download_full_text`, or `compacted_get_book_text`) to attempt to pull text from this title. Here's why that matters for you:\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Why This Matters Critically\n\nIf I were to use those tools and they returned text, that content could be:\n\n- **Fabricated by an underlying AI system** — some retrieval tools can generate plausible-sounding academic text rather than retrieve real documents.\n- **Completely invented** — including fake definitions of \"communicative silence,\" fake typologies, fake culture names, and fake citations that *sound* credible but have no basis in real scholarship.\n\nIf you included that material in a seminar paper, you could be submitting **fabricated academic content**, which is a serious academic integrity violation — even if you did so unknowingly.\n\n---\n\n## What I Recommend Instead\n\nIf you are researching **non-verbal communication and silence in Pacific cultures**, there is real, verifiable scholarship in this area. I can help you find it:\n\n1. **Search Google Scholar** for terms like *\"communicative silence\" Pacific cultures*, *non-verbal communication Polynesia/Melanesia/Micronesia*, or *silence typology cross-cultural*.\n2. **Real scholars** in adjacent fields include Adam Kendon (gesture/non-verbal communication), Deborah Tannen (silence in discourse), and researchers publishing in journals like *Oceania*, *The Journal of the Polynesian Society*, or *Language in Society*.\n3. **Ask your librarian** to run a verified search for the Tāwhiri title — if it exists, they will find it in WorldCat or a national library catalog.\n\nWould you like me to search for **real, verified sources** on non-verbal communication or silence typology in Pacific societies? I'm glad to help with that.",
